You can install jdb (the official Java Debug Wire Protocol CLI debugger included in default-jdk) alongside adb (for forwarding Android's jdwp:<pid> sockets) and jdwp-shellifier on Ubuntu 24.04 (noble).

1. Install jdb (default-jdk), adb, & nmap (Includes jdwp-exec / jdwp-info NSE Scripts)

bash
sudo apt update && sudo apt install -y default-jdk adb nmap python3 git
Use code with caution.
